Description: Make the thumbnails of a 3D clip from its left eye, and learn a packing only the stream says
 The bin's and the timeline's thumbnails of a 3D clip were the packed frame, both
 views squeezed into one picture. The thumbnail producer now gets MLT's
 stereo3d_unpack with output left, first of its filters, so a thumbnail is the
 left eye's view as one picture, at the shape of a view; frame sequences, one view
 per frame, are as before. A frame packing arrangement SEI is only read when a frame
 is decoded, so the clip learns its packing from the first thumbnail's frame, makes
 that thumbnail again from the left eye and updates its timeline producers; a render
 of a 3D project or with a 3D preset decodes one frame of each clip whose packing is
 not known yet, so a clip marked only in its stream is taken apart like the others.
 The thumbnail cache key of a 3D clip changes, so packed thumbnails cached earlier
 are not shown for it.
